Run the debounce tests from the repository root:

    pio test --project-conf test/platformio.ini -e native

The separate test configuration compiles lib/button/button.c unchanged on the
host. test/stubs/Arduino.h and hardware_stubs.cpp provide only the hardware
and BPM dependencies; the debounce implementation and Button objects come
from the production source. Each test resets state and installs counting
callbacks. No ESP32 is needed.

GitHub Actions runs this command on pushes, pull requests, and manual runs.
The nine tests cover the five-sample threshold, bounce rejection in both
directions, counter resets, held buttons, repeated presses, and independent
buttons. Physical button polarity, hardware timing, and RTOS scheduling are
outside this suite.

The old BPM tests referenced an obsolete two-argument step_increase /
step_decrease API. This suite currently covers debouncing only.
